%% 5.8 After-match — MVP, cover image & photos
%% Source of truth for this diagram. Rendered from ../specs/2026-08-03-events-feature-spec.md §5.8
%% Edit here, not in the spec — the spec links to this file.
sequenceDiagram
    actor O as Organizer
    participant API as Events API
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant IK as ImageKit

    Note over O,DB: status == 'after_match' for result and photos.<br/>The cover image is the exception — any state but 'done'.

    O->>API: POST /events/:id/result { mvpUserId }
    API->>API: assert organizer + status == 'after_match'
    API->>DB: look up EventPlayer(mvpUserId, status 'joined')
    alt MVP never joined this event
        API-->>O: 400 — the MVP must be a player who joined
        Note over API: naming a non-player would corrupt the<br/>profile mvpCount that parent §2.3 feeds
    else MVP is a joined player
        API->>DB: set result { mvpUserId, scoreA, scoreB }
        API-->>O: event with result
    end

    Note over O,IK: cover image — replaceable, so the old file must go

    O->>API: POST /events/:id/cover (multipart file)
    API->>IK: upload → { url, fileId }
    API->>DB: set coverImage + coverImageFileId
    API->>IK: delete the PREVIOUS fileId (best effort)
    Note over API,IK: deletion comes last and its failure is swallowed —<br/>an orphaned remote file beats losing the cover<br/>when the upload fails after a delete

    O->>API: POST /events/:id/photos (multipart file)
    API->>API: assert status == 'after_match'
    API->>IK: upload → { url, fileId }
    API->>DB: push { url, fileId } onto photos[]

    O->>API: DELETE /events/:id/photos/:fileId
    alt fileId is not on this event
        API-->>O: 404
    else found
        API->>DB: splice it out of photos[]
        API->>IK: delete the remote file (best effort)
        Note over API,IK: row first, file second — a failed remote<br/>delete leaks a file rather than leaving<br/>a broken URL on the event
    end
